	Configure which SPRT channel is used for data
apifn	sm_sprt_config_data_channel
params	sm_sprt_config_data_channel_parms configp
	The SPRT end point to configure.
field	tSMSPRTId sprt in
	The channel to use for data
field	int data_channel in
	The maximum length of the payload on the data channel
field	int max_payload_length in
	The data maximum latency
field	int max_latency in
unstruct
	Configures the channel used for data by the SPRT end point. The default
	is channel 3, but can be either 1 or 3.
	<p>
	A packet is filled with the data passed in via the datafeed and is sent 
	when it has reached the
ref	max_payload_length
	or it has had data for
ref	max_latency
	milliseconds.
explain
	0
retval
error   ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

